# Compulsory app standards

- Follow `APP-STANDARDS.md` for every app feature, fix, release and new project.
  It records the required branch, brand, platform support, launcher integration,
  UI, tray, notifications, themes, performance, Help, settings search, KB and
  crash-report acceptance criteria requested by the user.
- Treat all requirements as compulsory. Preserve established app-specific choices
  and existing instructions. Resolve any missing brand choice with the owner.
- Requirements are not evidence of implementation. Track outstanding work honestly;
  never claim a platform, feature or release is ready without verification.
- Include documentation, screenshots, functional tests and performance checks in
  relevant updates. Do not create unrelated product changes for policy-only edits.
- When creating a future app, copy this rule, `APP-STANDARDS.md`, and the existing
  security and KB maintenance guidance. Replace template identity fields with its
  real branch URL, name, KB prefix, approved colour and white icon choice.
- Follow `.cursor/rules/security-data.mdc`; no secrets or private data may be
  published. Preserve existing release/version approval requirements.
